		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">63</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">1. As there are 1000 rows it will be difficult for me to remember each row of the array, so I will take a paper and note down all the rows of 2D array.
2. Again I have to see through each row and look into diagonal elements and see if it is nrgative or not, if it is negative, I have to change it to -1 otherwise I have to change it to 1.

Hint: The diagonal elements will have row value same as the column value (e.g arr[0][0] or arr[5][5])</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">595.656717438214</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">4778.243240512852</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">348.4091545813991</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">254.482998015921</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">1. As there are 1000 rows it will be difficult for me to remember each row of the array, so I will take a paper and note down all the rows of 2D array.
2. Again I have to see through each row and look into diagonal elements and see if it is nrgative or not, if it is negative, I have to change it to -1 otherwise I have to change it to 1.

Hint: The diagonal elements will have row value same as the column value (e.g arr[0][0] or arr[5][5])</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontSize" type="int">12</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontName" type="String">Dialog</attribute>
				<attribute key="configuration" type="String">CroppingLabel</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentWidth" type="double">348.4091545813991</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentHeight" type="double">141.84375</attribute>
				<attribute key="autoSizePolicy" type="String">node_width</attribute>
				<attribute key="anchor" type="String">c</attribute>
			</section>
		</section>
		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">64</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">1. Read the length of 2D array from input
2. Create an empty array
3. Read the next row from input
4. Append it to the array
5. Repeat steps 3 and 4 until you read all rows of 2D array.
Phase 2
6. Now go to first row of 2D array.
7. Go to that element row value is equal to its column value and check if it is negative or not
7.1 If it is negative, then change it to 0.
7.2 Otherwise, change it to 1.
8. Move to next row.
9 Repeat step 7, 7.1, 7.2 and 8 untill we reach end of the array.
10. Go to first row of array.
11. Display that row, with elements are separated by spaces.
12. Move to next row.
13. Repeat steps 11 and 12 untill we reach end of the array.</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">314.8078816782776</attribute>
